#### x3-operator-read-through-eno-unwired — an operator box with EN read through its ENO writes its value somewhere (3c: it does not build)
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION LD
NETWORK
  x := MOVE 1 ENO EN c;
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_UNSUPPORTED an operator box read through its ENO with no output wired

#### x10-fb-with-eno-read-by-name — a box with EN and ENO read by an output stores and does not build (3b)
=== scope
instance c1 CTU
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION LD
NETWORK
  x := c1 : CTU(CU := a, PV := 10).CV ENO EN c;
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_UNSUPPORTED a box with EN and ENO read by its value

#### x12-eno-wired-beside-a-consumer — the ENO pin wired to a variable while a consumer reads the box (7b)
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION LD
NETWORK
  x := MOVE 7 => y ENO => lamp EN c;
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_UNSUPPORTED an ENO pin wired beside a consumer

#### x9-fb-read-through-named-eno — an FB's declared ENO is read with nothing after its call, never by `.ENO`
=== scope
instance d1 Dryer
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION LD
NETWORK
  ready := d1 : Dryer(iOn := on).`ENO`;
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_UNSUPPORTED an FB read through .ENO

#### x13-three-input-sub — SUB takes two inputs
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION FBD
NETWORK
  x := a SUB b SUB c;
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_UNSUPPORTED a two input operator box with more inputs

#### x13-three-input-gt — every comparison takes two
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION FBD
NETWORK
  x := a GT b GT c;
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_UNSUPPORTED a two input operator box with more inputs

#### x13-three-input-div-call-form — in the call form too
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION FBD
NETWORK
  x := `DIV`(a, b, NOT IN3 := c);
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_UNSUPPORTED a two input operator box with more inputs

#### x13-one-input-add — an operator takes at least two inputs
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION FBD
NETWORK
  x := `ADD`(a);
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_UNSUPPORTED an operator box with fewer than two inputs

#### x13-one-branch — a parallel with one branch does not compile (C0023)
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION LD
NETWORK
  x := s BRANCH (a);
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_UNSUPPORTED a Parallel with one branch

#### x17-split-defined-twice — a split is defined once
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION LD
NETWORK
  split1 := a;
  split1 := b;
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_DUPLICATE_NAME a split defined twice

#### x17-split-nested-twice — nested or not
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION LD
NETWORK
  split1 := a;
  x := (split1 := b);
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_DUPLICATE_NAME a split defined twice

#### split-never-defined — a split read is defined in its network
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION LD
NETWORK
  x := split7;
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_BAD_EXPRESSION a split referenced and never defined

#### split-reads-itself — a split read inside its own definition is not measured
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION LD
NETWORK
  split1 := a AND split1;
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_UNSUPPORTED a split read inside its own definition

#### split-leading-zero — a split's number is its VarId, no leading zeros
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION LD
NETWORK
  split01 := a;
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_BAD_EXPRESSION no leading zeros

#### split-coil-target — a split is never a coil target
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION LD
NETWORK
  x := split1 S= a;
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_BAD_EXPRESSION split1 as a coil target

#### split-output-target — never a `=>` target
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION LD
NETWORK
  MOVE a => split1;
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_BAD_EXPRESSION with no target

#### split-call-head — never a call head
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION LD
NETWORK
  x := split1(IN := a);
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_BAD_EXPRESSION is a split, never a call head

#### measure-negated-jump — a modified jump is not measured
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION LD
NETWORK
  NOT JMP Done := c;
END_NETWORK
NETWORK LABEL: Done
  ;
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_UNSUPPORTED a modified jump or return

#### measure-reset-jump — R= on a jump is not measured
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION LD
NETWORK
  JMP Done R= c;
END_NETWORK
NETWORK LABEL: Done
  ;
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_UNSUPPORTED a modified jump or return

#### measure-rising-return — an edge on a return is not measured
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION LD
NETWORK
  R_EDGE RETURN := c;
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_UNSUPPORTED a modified jump or return

#### measure-edge-set-coil — an edge beside S= is not measured
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION LD
NETWORK
  R_EDGE x S= c;
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_UNSUPPORTED an edge beside a set or reset coil

#### measure-modified-coil-beside-another — a negated or edge coil beside another coil is not measured
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION LD
NETWORK
  NOT x := y := c;
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_UNSUPPORTED a modified coil beside another coil

#### measure-negated-empty-beside-a-coil — `NOT;` beside another coil is not measured
=== text
IMPLEMENTATION LD
NETWORK
  x := y := NOT;
END_NETWORK
=== refused
NETWORK_UNSUPPORTED a negated empty slot outside a lone coil value

#### measure-negated-empty-on-a-set-coil — `x S= NOT;` is not measured
